<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net11.0</TargetFramework>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Include="..\..\..\..\..\target\debug\*reference_project*">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
    </Content>
  </ItemGroup>
  <!--
      The Content glob above copies the native library these bindings P/Invoke into. It is
      correct as written: a top-level `cargo build -p reference_project` puts the cdylib in
      target\debug. Verified 2026-08-27 - do not "fix" the path. Building the crate only as a
      test dependency leaves an unhashed copy in target\debug\deps with no hardlink up, which
      is why the directory can look empty.

      Provisioning is deliberately NOT done from MSBuild. An Exec running cargo here contends
      with any other cargo holding the target directory lock; observed 2026-08-27 as
      `failed to create file target\debug\reference_project.d`, cargo exit 101, in a plain
      `dotnet build` with no outer cargo at all. Under `cargo test` it would block rather than
      fail. Provision on the cargo side: build the crate with every feature enabled before
      building or testing this project.

      A fail-fast guard was attempted 2026-08-27 and removed. Hooked to
      BeforeTargets="PrepareForBuild", it did not fire on an up-to-date project - that target is
      skipped, and the guard with it. If you retry, hook something that always runs and verify it
      fires in BOTH directions before trusting it. Until then the failure mode is
      DllNotFoundException from the Interop static constructor, which looks like a marshalling
      fault and is not.

      The all-features flag is not optional: the bindings are generated with every feature
      enabled, so a narrower build produces EntryPointNotFoundException, which looks like an
      interop bug and is a build-configuration one. See docs/csharp-unions-handoff.md section 9.
    -->
</Project>